c c_src/CMakeLists.txt\n```\n\nThe search has no matches. `main` has one unconditional `return 0`, which is\nthe normal success result rather than a rejection.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n\nThere are no C rejection branches. Scanner conversion failure and EOF are not\nreported as errors: `scanf`'s return is ignored, the initialized `+0.0` remains\nin place, `driver(+0.0)` runs, and `main` returns `0`. Those observable paths\nare covered as valid behavior in `CONFIGS.md`.\n\nGeneric FFI boundary applicability:\n\n| Entry point | Null pointers | Lengths | Enums/ranges |\n|-------------|---------------|---------|--------------|\n| `driver(double)` | not applicable | not applicable | all 64-bit `double` representations are exercised |\n| `main(void)` | not applicable | empty/invalid/overflowing stdin forms are exercised | not applicable |\n\n# Configuration Surface\n\n## Build-Time Configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no\noptions, conditional sources, compile definitions, or preprocessor feature\nselection. There is exactly one valid build configuration:\n\n| # | Cargo features | C configuration | Check command | Status |\n|---|----------------|-----------------|---------------|--------|\n| 1 | none (`--no-default-features`) | default | `cargo check --no-default-features` | [x] |\n\n## Runtime Axes\n\nThe C source has two public entry points and no explicit `if`, `switch`, or\npreprocessor branches. Its observable data-shape distinctions come from:\n\n- `driver(double)`: raw IEEE-754 bits plus `%a` and `%.4f` formatting.\n- `main(void)`: `%lf` scanning into an initialized `+0.0`, followed by\n  `driver`.\n\nThe following is the pruned cross-product of entry point, IEEE-754 class, and\nscanner subject-sequence form. Scanner failure and EOF are included because C\ncontinues successfully with initialized state rather than rejecting them.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `driver` | direct call; positive and negative zero bit patterns | [ ] |\n| 2 | `driver` | direct call; positive and negative finite subnormals, including boundary payloads | [ ] |\n| 3 | `driver` | direct call; positive and negative finite normals, including exponent/mantissa boundaries | [ ] |\n| 4 | `driver` | direct call; positive and negative infinity | [ ] |\n| 5 | `driver` | direct call; positive/negative quiet and signaling NaNs with varied payloads | [ ] |\n| 6 | `main` -> `driver` | decimal finite normal/zero subject sequences, with signs and exponents | [ ] |\n| 7 | `main` -> `driver` | decimal finite subnormal and signed-zero subject sequences | [ ] |\n| 8 | `main` -> `driver` | hexadecimal finite normal/subnormal subject sequences | [ ] |\n| 9 | `main` -> `driver` | case-varied infinity subject sequences | [ ] |\n| 10 | `main` -> `driver` | case-varied NaN subject sequences, with accepted payload forms | [ ] |\n| 11 | `main` -> `driver` | decimal overflow subject sequences | [ ] |\n| 12 | `main` -> `driver` | decimal underflow subject sequences | [ ] |\n| 13 | `main` -> `driver` | accepted number with varied leading whitespace and trailing bytes | [ ] |\n| 14 | `main` -> `driver` | nonempty conversion-failure subject sequence; initialized `+0.0` is used | [ ] |\n| 15 | `main` -> `driver` | empty stdin/EOF; initialized `+0.0` is used | [ ] |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
